# tests/pins/k0.sha256 -- sha256 of K0 as hex0-seed assembles kernel/k0/k0.hex0
# (1,453 bytes).  kernel/k0/check.sh compares.  When a change to k0.hex0 is
# meant to alter it, update this line in the same commit and say why.
#   1,313 bytes, 40da2915...: K0 before the hex0 hand-off.
#   1,435 bytes, fb2093a3...: call 248 writes a file to the IDE disk by PIO
#   (boot 1 of tests/tinycc/hex0-handoff-check.sh writes builder-hex0's
#   disk with it), and execve zeroes the new stack's 8 MiB, as Linux's
#   fresh pages are, so a program reading stack it never wrote (tcc -g's
#   getcwd buffer) sees what it sees on Linux.
#   1,461 bytes, fc738003...: brk (12), for Mes libc's malloc in the
#   first tcc, grows the loaded image's end and zeroes what it adds.
#   1,453 bytes: k0.hex0 written directly, with no NASM source; 8 bytes of
#   hand optimisation, behaviour unchanged (execve's redundant mov edi,
#   SP0; brk returns through xchg, not push/pop; read's count in one mov;
#   execve counts argv from -1).
f8623b11b9b001611a2de3cd450837ac977deff3850272213f4240357519cfc0  k0.bin
